"## Summary\n\nAgent-core follow-up 48: review r28's H-1 (isolation F20-01), review r27's H-1, M-1 and L-1, and the R23 boot-heartbeat flake.\n- **Session:** launched 20:51 EST on 2026-11-03, and delivered at 21:28.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 8 commits and 19 owned files, +1,995/\u221227.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: current `main` (`a4390094`, after #446) with this branch and enrollment 10 merged in. All pass:\n    - `make node-lint node-test node-test-integration node-build`;\n    - the r27 and r28 proofs in `node/agent` and `node/enforce`, 10 tests;\n    - the lock's consumers: `go test ./node/updater/... ./node/nodelock/... ./node/internal/nodelock/...`;\n    - `make -f mk/e2e.mk e2e-lint`, `at-enrollment-lint` and `at-isolation-lint`;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...` and the committed-evidence tests;\n    - `make go-lint`, `go vet ./...`, gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n- **Scope:** one ordinary lab in the lane's own prefix, with no rerun and no reservation. Zero owned Docker objects at the end.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **Five confirmed defects, each fixed, each with its imported proof failing before and passing after:**\n  - **r28 H-1, isolation's F20-01** (`12ced44a`). The tunnel probe ran on the step's control budget, so control requests that hung until that budget ran out made the probe fail at once. The node withdrew itself about 5 s after control loss, long before its lease ended. Introduced by #429. Local work, the probe and the usage store's lock now run on a local work context.\n  - **r27 H-1** (`0d04972d`). At boot, before NetBird creates the member interface, its absence was read as a foreign filter. That latched `TC_FOREIGN_FILTER`, D-106 containment evidence and a quarantine. Absence now needs a successful independent link inventory. A real foreign filter is still contained.\n  - **r27 M-1** (`fbabb131`). After a D-136 closed-recovery Apply, the agent waited past its renewal slot, and installed a redundant `awaiting_member_grants` baseline. The grant-less deadline now schedules the Step, and the verified deny-all model is retained while it waits.\n  - **r27 L-1** (`543106ca`). One Step could run two quarantines and four baselines. Now there is one containment attempt per local pass, and its verified baseline is reused until the next rules mutation.\n  - **R23's boot heartbeat** (`ad0894a2`). A 100 ms child deadline made ordinary disk or scheduler delay look like a startup failure. The heartbeat now uses Boot's own deadline, and the expiry check before publication stays.\n- **The six Held proofs still pass.** D-150's requested code reading is \"not determined\", and the dated note says why.\n- **The ordinary lab: 12 pass, 1 fail, 1 optional skip.** The failure is `TestLabD087_D104_GrantRenewalExpiryCorrelation`'s last-positive lower bound: forwarding stopped 2.86 s before the lease's deadline D, and the bound is 101 ms. The lane assigned no cause.\n- **The orchestrator's reading of that failure: F48-01, a restart race, not a regression of this branch.** From the retained captures:\n  - the lab restarts the agent 3 s before D, with lease requests held. The old process logs `serving rules retained for restart`;\n  - about 10.6 ms later, a heartbeat with generation 0, `serving` false and `baseline_ok` false appears. That matches the successor's startup heartbeat, which Boot publishes before any stage can block (r22 M-3, #429);\n  - 8.4 ms after it, the watchdog takes the lock, decides `baseline_unverified`, and writes a baseline, 2.83 s before D;\n  - the successor's adoption then fails with `GENERATION_MISMATCH`, and the node stays closed until D.\n  - **This branch does not change that mechanism.** Its only change to the startup heartbeat removes the 100 ms cap. Isolation's ISO-F6-03 on 2026-10-31 had the same signature, and was never attributed.\n- **D-156 (orchestrator, provisional; Ted may overturn):** a same-boot process replacement keeps a verified retained ruleset until the successor adopts or refuses it. A stalled successor stays bounded by the watchdog's staleness and the kernel timeout at D.\n  - Agent-core 49 fixes F48-01 under D-156, together with F30-01's Boot changes: `recoverOnce` runs inside the same window today.\n  - Members 21 and isolation 21 are told how to recognise its signature, so a restart race is not counted against r27 H-1.\n- **Routed by the report:**\n  - the whole-control outage with hanging requests, as a lab scenario, to netlab;\n  - the acceptance runs, to isolation 21, members 21 and security-ops 16. They start when this merges.\n"
